@@ -125,5 +125,6 @@
 | D-145 | Kritva Connect is registered as a planned workstream `CONNECT` with repository `KritvaOS/kritva-connect`, its ten architecture decision records (CONNECT-ADR-01 to CONNECT-ADR-10) are recorded as accepted, and its tasks KOS-CONNECT-001 to KOS-CONNECT-010 enter the planning inventory as PLANNING_ONLY (Dinesh, chat, 2026-11-22: confirmed the public/private repository split, then "I approve D1-D12 and PR 1 and PR 2 as branches for review", after reviewing a plan on which Claude and an external AI reviewer, advisory only, aligned) | The seven-repository register (D-109) has no row for realtime connectivity (LiveKit audio, video, telemetry and operator input between robots, simulators and the platform), and the RaaS WebRTC and signaling tasks that might overlap could not be located. A provider-neutral Connect layer with a thin gateway keeps LiveKit credentials out of public code and keeps command authority in RaaS and on the robot | `workstreams.json` gains `CONNECT` with its repository. `planning_inventory.json` gains one REGISTERED group pinned to `planning/TASKS.md` of kritva-connect at commit 2753390ef8b70617bee20deba465667c09edd6e9 (sha256 144b3bee7b76937cc5340b5d5dbd1c6c0a2d4b4b42da7002d8f12e5f1ceb026a). The tasks carry no weight, have no baseline entry, approval or credit, and any baseline entry later needs a non-zero weight and its own owner decision (D-109). The ten ADRs live in kritva-connect `docs/adr/` and were accepted in chat only. They include work that Connect does not own and that is not registered: device enrollment, a device-authenticated token endpoint, a control-lease service and revocation belong to RaaS, and where the Control Plane lives must be reconciled with D-144 first. A Security Owner review is required before KOS-CONNECT-003 is accepted. The repository count becomes eight (D-144 says a count change needs its own owner decision and a register re-plan before V2-M3, 2027-03-15): this decision adds no `repo-pipeline.json` entry, no milestone rows, no dependency or risk rows, and does not change `V2_REPO_PLAN.md`; those are separate changes. A separate private deployment repository exists and is deliberately not named in this record. `kritva-sdk` and `kritva-sim` are not registered (D-144). Not verified: that the KR-FE-3 and KR-BE-6 RaaS tasks do or do not overlap Connect | Open (accepted when the owner merges this pull request) |
